# Div-split (error-model.md §11 Increment 2 (C)): a single signed Div has TWO
# fault categories. `INT_MIN / -1` is an OVERFLOW (Fault.Overflow), NOT a
# div-by-zero; `10 / 0` is Fault.DivByZero. The binding form reads the right
# variant for each, and the pattern forms catch the right category. Rem too.
void main():
    int imin = -9223372036854775807 - 1
    int neg1 = -1
    # INT_MIN / -1 → Fault.Overflow (binding reads the variant).
    int a = (imin / neg1) catch f: match f:
        case Fault.Overflow(): 1
        case Fault.DivByZero(): 2
        case Fault.Bounds(): 3
    print(f"{a}")
    # INT_MIN / -1 caught by the Overflow pattern.
    int b = (imin / neg1) catch Fault.Overflow: 11
    print(f"{b}")
    # 10 / 0 still caught by DivByZero.
    int z = 0
    int c = (10 / z) catch Fault.DivByZero: 22
    print(f"{c}")
    # INT_MIN % -1 is the same overflow.
    int d = (imin % neg1) catch Fault.Overflow: 33
    print(f"{d}")
